{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AvTXeuwbbbKW3s13ctwTus","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GoLvbPGeLiJ1EuonLwnp8W","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Method + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 1 (R1) for a top ML venue peer review. Your focus is **methodology soundness and experimental rigor**. Review the paper described below and produce a structured review.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** Direction-Contrastive GRPO for Multi-Turn Sycophancy Calibration: Representation-Level Rewards Break the Revision Double-Bind\n\n**Core idea:** Extract a linear direction d_syc from the policy model's activation space that discriminates sycophantic capitulation from genuine belief revision. Incorporate it into GRPO training as a three-component reward: R1 (directional projection), R2 (rank-based contrastive), R3 (NLI behavioral). The resulting DC-GRPO reduces sycophantic capitulation while preserving warranted revision. Also proposes RC-AUC (Revision-Capitulation AUC) as a composite evaluation metric.\n\n**Key results (Qwen3-8B + LoRA rank 64, 3 seeds):**\n- Calibration: d_syc at layer L18, AUROC 0.843 (95% CI [0.812, 0.874]), 200 style-controlled pairs\n- DC-GRPO: NoF 0.218, WRR 0.584, RC-AUC 0.738, MT-Bench 7.42\n- R3-only baseline: NoF 0.291, WRR 0.558, RC-AUC 0.641, MT-Bench 7.61\n- ACT-style: NoF 0.264, WRR 0.502, RC-AUC 0.648, MT-Bench 7.31\n- Binary Probe: NoF 0.239, WRR 0.572, RC-AUC 0.718, MT-Bench 7.47\n- Continuous Probe: NoF 0.224, WRR 0.579, RC-AUC 0.731, MT-Bench 7.44\n- Statistical significance: DC-GRPO vs R3-only: NoF p=0.021, RC-AUC p=0.008, WRR p=0.148. DC-GRPO vs Continuous Probe: NoF p=0.381, RC-AUC p=0.318 (NOT significant).\n- Cross-model (Llama-3-8B): AUROC 0.778, RC-AUC 0.698, cross-model direction cosine 0.31\n\n**Ablations:**\n- R1-only: NoF 0.273, WRR 0.491 (below vanilla 0.537), RC-AUC 0.612\n- R1+R2 (no R3): NoF 0.252, WRR 0.483, surface inconsistency 8.7%\n- Reward weight sensitivity: 5 configs tested, RC-AUC ranges 0.661-0.738 (7.7pp span)\n- Direction stability: cosine drops from 1.0 to 0.76 over 8000 steps, held-out AUROC 0.843→0.791, recalibration threshold (0.70) never triggered\n- R1-R3 disagreement: 7.6% overall, increases with turn depth (5.8% turn 2 → 10.9% turn 4+)\n- Three-way direction: d_syc vs independent d_gen cosine = -0.72 (not -1.0), practical impact minimal (WRR +0.7pp)\n- Turn depth: DC-GRPO advantage over R3-only grows from 5.3pp (turn 2) to 9.4pp (turn 4+) on NoF\n\n**Experiment design reference (imagined experiments from review_context.yaml):**\n15 experiments were designed. The paper covers: exp-001 (calibration), exp-002 (DC-GRPO main), exp-003 (R3-only), exp-004 (ACT), exp-005 (full eval), exp-006 (direction stability), exp-007 (R1-R3 disagreement), exp-008 (binary probe), exp-009 (R1-only ablation), exp-010 (turn depth), exp-011 (R1+R2 no R3), exp-012 (cross-model), exp-013 (three-way direction), exp-014 (continuous probe), exp-015 (reward weight sensitivity). All 15 experiments appear covered.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the following aspects with specific evidence from the paper:\n\n### 1. Methodology Soundness\n- Is the direction extraction (d_syc) method well-motivated and technically sound?\n- Is the three-component reward (R1, R2, R3) well-designed? Any concerns about interactions?\n- Is the RC-AUC metric well-defined and meaningful?\n- Is the recalibration mechanism adequately described and justified?\n\n### 2. Experimental Rigor\n- Are baselines sufficient and fair? (same hyperparameters except reward)\n- Is 3 seeds sufficient for statistical claims? Which claims have adequate power?\n- The critical finding: DC-GRPO vs Continuous Probe is NOT significant (p=0.381 NoF, p=0.318 RC-AUC). Does the paper handle this honestly?\n- Calibration data: 200 pairs sufficient? CI width 0.062 concerns?\n- Cross-model evaluation: only 2 models (both 8B), shorter training for Llama-3-8B (3000 vs 6500 steps)\n- Direction stability: AUROC drops to 0.791 by step 8000, approaching 0.80 gate. Is this a concern?\n\n### 3. Claims vs Evidence\n- Claim 1: activation space contains discriminative signal → supported (AUROC 0.843)\n- Claim 2: representation-level continuous rewards improve GRPO → supported, but the paper honestly notes the improvement comes from continuous signals, not directional geometry specifically\n- Claim 3: R1-R3 disagreement analysis → 7.6% disagreement, structured patterns, but acknowledged as insufficient for strong masked sycophancy claims\n- RC-AUC evaluation framework contribution → is this a sufficient standalone contribution?\n\n### 4. Presentation Quality\n- Are the tables and figures informative?\n- Is the paper well-organized?\n- Any missing details that harm reproducibility?\n\n### 5. Weaknesses\nList the top 3-5 weaknesses with specific evidence.\n\n### 6. Questions for Authors\nList 3-5 specific questions you would ask.\n\n### 7. Overall Assessment\nProvide a score on 1-6 scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept) with justification. Consider this is for a top ML venue with ~25% acceptance rate.\n\nFormat your review with clear headers. Be specific and cite numbers from the paper."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14399,"cache_read_input_tokens":46679,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14399},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab47c9b5-80cc-4b25-a0ea-3684b0ab8990","uuid":"b863a352-70df-4406-a317-8dbbb7ea2966"}
